    {
      "id": "03-fats",
      "index": 2,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "fats",
      "text": "13 grams of fat. Omega 3 is 2200 milligrams, which is a huge strength here. Saturated fat is 3.1 grams, so the fat profile stays pretty clean for a meat. For meats, fat quality is the main tradeoff, and salmon handles that really well.",
      "textSha256": "1013b34192df24806ae367a5026d3ce792b24bc03420f04ca0c752be3260782f",
      "characterCount": 235,
      "byteLength": 224906,
      "mediaDurationSeconds": 14.028,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/salmon/voice-v1-blocks/03-fats.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "mhHyXRvjJWe7wEzFDLiH",
        "historyItemId": "GUZHHhBpdhC5WNU7oOze"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/salmon/voice/voice-v1-blocks/03-fats.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-carbs",
      "index": 3,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "carbs",
      "text": "No defensible carb submacros to call out. For meats, carbs barely matter unless something has been added, so this section is basically neutral.",
      "textSha256": "a933436b880e470252af9d5ed60845f4a18e830e244f191b61377a0f91b93c83",
      "characterCount": 143,
      "byteLength": 112475,
      "mediaDurationSeconds": 7.001,
