        "historyItemId": "WaMnUxNEtpQIVOyjjIuE"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/salmon/voice/voice-v1-blocks/04-carbs.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-proteins",
      "index": 4,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "proteins",
      "text": "20.4 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 9 out of 9, and nonessential amino acids score is 10 out of 11, so the protein quality is strong. Collagen is only 0.3 grams, so the structural-protein side is weak. For meats, complete protein matters a lot, and the 94% bio availability does bring it back up a lot too.",
      "textSha256": "aa3d2e7e53768d9853ccbaf529b645cd3fe0dd6be654c3b1fefb4620cf472567",
      "characterCount": 324,
      "byteLength": 305572,
      "mediaDurationSeconds": 19.069,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/salmon/voice-v1-blocks/05-proteins.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "NaW59ABkOn1lAU35pHTw",
        "historyItemId": "xvJAwNTff8HvH4HmoRFC"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/salmon/voice/voice-v1-blocks/05-proteins.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-vitamins",
      "index": 5,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "vitamins",
      "text": "Vitamin B12 is 117% daily value, which is excellent for nerve and blood-cell support. Vitamin D is 66% daily value, which is also a serious mark for bone and immune support. Vitamin C is 0, but for meats, B12 and vitamin D matter much more.",
      "textSha256": "b6c8a7c7626dfae60907a9d51943addddbe643a66e21e50279904943095b7ead",
      "characterCount": 240,
      "byteLength": 246222,
      "mediaDurationSeconds": 15.36,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/salmon/voice-v1-blocks/06-vitamins.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "1kcPSXwr04M6OJ2KCa5I",
        "historyItemId": "jO1xbVJ9PTyep5XlkMF4"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/salmon/voice/voice-v1-blocks/06-vitamins.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-minerals",
      "index": 6,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "minerals",
      "text": "Minerals are the weak section. Potassium is 8% daily value, which is the best number here but still low. Iron is only 4% daily value, and zinc is only 4% too. For meats, minerals can add value, but salmon is not winning through this section.",
      "textSha256": "fdbe00ffd850cee45fe0db3a99ed6d28e02477deb0e0f020ac702bfe170ce08a",
      "characterCount": 241,
      "byteLength": 219472,
      "mediaDurationSeconds": 13.688,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/salmon/voice-v1-blocks/07-minerals.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "7uBwHlnwHmZzuiXoxz59",
        "historyItemId": "TdSG7n6MhHJermtM8zXj"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/salmon/voice/voice-v1-blocks/07-minerals.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-pros",
      "index": 7,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "pros",
      "text": "The upsides first: easy to build a strong meal around. Works as a real centrepiece food. Helps meals feel complete. Very useful when you want protein without needing lots of extras. Strong healthy-food reputation. In this case, the reputation actually matches the numbers.",
      "textSha256": "4e1069458b9c1462a8bbb132b0fac8feff1f5796a676f16caa4f46e14da58ba1",
      "characterCount": 272,
      "byteLength": 251655,
      "mediaDurationSeconds": 15.7,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/salmon/voice-v1-blocks/08-pros.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "MuGHacouhYkxKOgolyAb",
        "historyItemId": "7XRjCIGiih6kugBNAlXa"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/salmon/voice/voice-v1-blocks/08-pros.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-cons",
      "index": 8,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "cons",
      "text": "Cons next: can be expensive. Price can make it less practical. Quality varies with sourcing. Wild, farmed, fresh, and frozen versions can shift the real-world result. Needs good storage and handling. It is not as easy as shelf-stable protein.",
      "textSha256": "5ab3189077abffd62e31d9fc79733b9794d79657d0852a3cf3ae86fa93f8f7da",
      "characterCount": 242,
      "byteLength": 224070,
      "mediaDurationSeconds": 13.976,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/salmon/voice-v1-blocks/09-cons.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "4kZ9QZVFWN7FdKAnJwVA",
        "historyItemId": "1M00pvs0Vi9v7c3pLPCN"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/salmon/voice/voice-v1-blocks/09-cons.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-closing_summary",
      "index": 9,
      "kind": "closing_summary",
      "sectionKey": null,
      "text": "Best bits are omega 3, vitamin B12, vitamin D, and complete protein. Weak spots are the low minerals, and the practical issues around price, sourcing, and storage. Best as a protein-and-fat source for heart health, muscle support, bone support, immune support, and practical high-protein meals.",
      "textSha256": "2943118f99c5caf91f0b724c9ed1068ee1b80edd56bf36d48e39bd9febb44e47",
